ent composition can vary based on your team's playstyle and the specific situation, here are some popular and effective combinations for the Abyss map: Standard Meta Composition: Duelist:  Jett or Raze Initiator:  Breach or Fade Controller:  Omen or Harbor Sentinel:  Killjoy or Cypher This composition offers a good balance of aggression, information gathering, map control, and site defense. Aggressive Playstyle: Duelist:  Jett or Raze Initiator:  Breach or Neon Controller:  Omen or Harbor Sentinel:  Killjoy or Cypher This comp focuses on fast-paced aggression with strong entry fraggers and map control abilities. Control-Oriented Playstyle: Duelist:  Reyna or Phoenix Initiator:  Sova or Skye Controller:  Omen or Viper Sentinel:  Killjoy or Cypher This composition emphasizes map control and information gathering, with a focus on defensive play. Hybrid Composition: Duelist:  Jett or Raze Initiator:  Fade or Gekko Controller:  Harbor or Viper Sentinel:  Cypher or Chamber This comp offers flexibility, allowing you to adapt to different situations. It combines aggression, information gathering, and map control. Key Considerations for Team Composition: Map Control:  Agents like Omen, Viper, and Harbor excel at controlling areas and chokepoints. Information Gathering:  Agents like Sova, Fade, and Cypher provide valuable intel about enemy positions.    Entry Fragging:  Duelists like Jett and Raze are crucial for taking control of sites. Utility:  Agents like Breach, Skye, and Killjoy offer essential utility for team success. Remember: These are just general recommendations. The best composition depends on your team's strengths, weaknesses, and preferences. Communication and coordination are essential for any team composition to succeed. Be prepared to adapt your composition based on the enemy team's lineup and the current state of the game. By carefully selecting your agents and working together as a team, you can maximize your chances of success on the Abyss map."}